{"publication":"24594","pdfSha256":"e18bd39ad0ca19d2eb9b9ea25c2635144c5ab368e5d6fbdc7a08345515ea1aee","pdfPage":293,"layoutPage":"                                     [AMD Public Use]\n\n24594—Rev. 3.38—July 2026                                                       AMD64 Technology\n\n\n\n\nMOVDIR64B                                                   Move 64B as Direct Store\nMoves 64-bytes as direct-store from a source memory address to a 64-byte aligned destination\nmemory address with 64-byte write atomicity. The destination address is specified in the register\noperand as offset in the ES segment and must be 64-byte aligned. The source address does not have\nalignment requirements.\nMOVDIR64B uses:\n   • write-combining (WC) memory type if the base destination memory type is non-coherent\n     (uncacheable (UC) or WC)\n   • write-combining plus (WC+) memory type if the base destination memory type is coherent\n     (write-back (WB), write-through (WT), write-protect (WP), or cache disable (CD)).\nMOVDIR64B uses the weakly-ordered WC or WC+ memory type even if the base memory type is\nstronger ordering. MOVDIRI will allocate a new write-combining buffer (WCB) and will not combine\nwith any WCBs from older instructions. The new WCB will be evicted before it is combined with\nyounger stores.\nThe MOVDIR64B instruction is weakly-ordered with respect to other stores. Software should use the\nSFENCE or MFENCE instruction to force strong memory ordering of MOVDIR64B with respect to\nother memory instructions.\nThe 64B load from the source has no atomicity guarantee and may require more than one load\noperation to complete. The 64-byte store is guaranteed to be an atomic write to the destination,\nproviding write-completion atomicity.\nSupport for the MOVDIR64B                     instruction       is    indicated        by     CPUID\nFn0000_0007_ECX_x0[MOVDIR64B] = 1.\n\nInstruction Encoding\n\nMnemonic                       Opcode         Description\n                                66 0F 3B F8   Direct store of 64-bit value from general purpose\n MOVDIR64B mem512, reg64        /r            register to memory.\n\nRelated Instructions\nMOVDIRI\n\nrFLAGS Affected\nNone\n\n\n\n\nGeneral-Purpose                                                                                   251\nInstruction Reference\n","cells":[{"id":"pdf:293:cell:0","pdfPage":293,"rect":[251.151489,4.09422,360.846489,23.20422],"wordSpan":[0,3],"wordBoxesSha256":"ed9e5522e2d0355c23d3fc390d480afdc96221e75c81b889abc30b06c4ed7943","unicodeSha256":"cb9a32cb7cda694a9471249208941a694cc0a803969c2bac64dd553086c94897","text":"[AMD Public Use]","wordBoxes":[{"text":"[AMD","rect":[251.151489,4.09422,286.151489,23.20422]},{"text":"Public","rect":[290.041489,4.09422,328.163489,23.20422]},{"text":"Use]","rect":[332.062489,4.09422,360.846489,23.20422]}],"glyphSpan":null,"glyphEvidence":"not-extracted: source is Unicode word boxes"},{"id":"pdf:293:cell:1","pdfPage":293,"rect":[62.9874,45.6171,212.1023,60.9511],"wordSpan":[3,6],"wordBoxesSha256":"da09886a012f13c9fcbd8a5ce1324f5cc403c4c16c1185db9c5cf4db3287fb6e","unicodeSha256":"aaf564d78c1add333e5bd48fe8c3a2f7cbdc1f6bf77a0a5898e45dd31c057d08","text":"24594—Rev. 3.38—July 2026","wordBoxes":[{"text":"24594—Rev.","rect":[62.9874,45.6171,127.0712,60.9511]},{"text":"3.38—July","rect":[130.1754,45.6171,184.5033,60.9511]},{"text":"2026","rect":[187.5074,45.6171,212.1023,60.9511]}],"glyphSpan":null,"glyphEvidence":"not-extracted: source is Unicode word boxes"},{"id":"pdf:293:cell:2","pdfPage":293,"rect":[447.4594,45.6171,549.0972,60.9511],"wordSpan":[6,8],"wordBoxesSha256":"bddc76e0f0ac940ebef6e8b4b9eb2d20576cb41dd3be08453a9d50fe5282821c","unicodeSha256":"70e213c4a31748f9f77a863ce4e1e49ee9ff8122a32f47b46615b19d2f2bc8c7","text":"AMD64 Technology","wordBoxes":[{"text":"AMD64","rect":[447.4594,45.6171,484.7736,60.9511]},{"text":"Technology","rect":[487.7777,45.6171,549.0972,60.9511]}],"glyphSpan":null,"glyphEvidence":"not-extracted: source